  GoP give +3 to hit directly, unlike GoDex which have to be enchanted
and then translated through the Dex ability.  Str 25 gives +6 damage
bonus, +4 more than Str:18/74 or less.  Think of GoP as a +4 ring of
increase damage with no nutrition cost, doesn't take up a ring slot,
can't be destroyed by shock, and gives a point of AC.

  +3 to-hit and +6 total damage bonus look perfect for you, or indeed,
most characters.  As you point out, the only downside is the effect on
spellcasting.  Unless casting spells at melee range is critical, this
can easily be avoided by taking one turn to remove the GoP, then cast
the spell, then take one turn to wear the GoP again.

  For a monk, they'll turn shuriken in deadly weapons.  A +0 shuriken at
basic skill with Str:25 will average 10 damage at ranges up to 11.
(Even worthless glass will average 8.)  Enchant the shuriken to +7 and
that's +17 damage at ranges up to 11.  Bless them and get your luck
maximized and they'll last.  Heck, even unskilled blessed darts will do
a lot of damage if you throw early and often with str:25.


